# Event director and World's Favor (events/*.js, design/data/events.toml). Every `ttl events expect ...` prints
# "ttl: ..." when it does not hold, which `server.sh test-all` counts as a failure.
# Expect in the log: "[ttl] events: omen started [manual]" / "omen ended (manual)", "[ttl] events: omen started (2 min)"
# (the scheduler pass), "[ttl] favor: TtlBotEvB is offered ...", "[ttl] favor: TtlBotEvB received tensura:...", and
# "[ttl] events: favor started for TtlBotEvA". Test bots never reach Discord (no #story line is posted for them).
ttlbot spawn TtlBotEvA
ttlbot spawn TtlBotEvB
ttlbot spawn TtlBotEvC
@sleep 3
# Start from a quiet director: an event left running from before the run (a Blood Moon a player saw, a manual fire) would
# break the counts below. Scheduled starts ignore test bots, so nothing new starts during the run on its own.
ttl events end
ttl events
# Sample event "omen": manual only; its declarative action turns spectatorsGenerateChunks off while it runs.
ttl events expect registered omen false
ttl events expect scheduled omen false
ttl events expect active none
ttl events expect rule spectatorsGenerateChunks true
ttl events fire omen
ttl events expect active omen
ttl events expect count 1
ttl events expect rule spectatorsGenerateChunks false
ttl events end omen
ttl events expect active none
ttl events expect rule spectatorsGenerateChunks true
# The scheduler: `due` makes the event due, one pass for it starts it (omen is exempt from the daily cap; `tick omen` lets the
# test bots count as online and leaves every other due event alone), `end` without an id ends all.
ttl events due omen
ttl events tick omen
ttl events expect active omen
ttl events expect scheduled omen false
ttl events end
ttl events expect active none
ttl events expect rule spectatorsGenerateChunks true
ttl events next
# Mute: chat lines off for one player, titles stay.
execute as TtlBotEvA run ttl events mute
ttl events expect muted TtlBotEvA true
execute as TtlBotEvA run ttl events mute
ttl events expect muted TtlBotEvA false
# World's Favor: A has 100 EP and 6 h, B 50 EP and 6 h, C 20 EP but only 1 h (not active enough). B is the lowest eligible.
ttl events clear TtlBotEvA
ttl events clear TtlBotEvB
ttl events clear TtlBotEvC
ttl events setup TtlBotEvA 100 6
ttl events setup TtlBotEvB 50 6
ttl events setup TtlBotEvC 20 1
ttl events fire favor
ttl events expect winner TtlBotEvB
ttl events expect offer TtlBotEvB true
ttl events expect offer TtlBotEvA false
ttl events expect offer TtlBotEvC false
ttl events expect cooldown TtlBotEvB true
# The offer is 3 random blessings; pin it so the pick below is deterministic, then choose a Common unique (registry).
ttl events offerset TtlBotEvB ep_surge,common_unique,protection
# A blessing that is not on offer is refused and nothing is consumed.
execute as TtlBotEvB run ttl favor choose relic
ttl events expect offer TtlBotEvB true
execute as TtlBotEvB run ttl favor choose common_unique
ttl events expect unique TtlBotEvB true
ttl events expect offer TtlBotEvB false
ttl registry expect pending TtlBotEvB 0
# B is on cooldown and C is not active enough: A is next.
ttl events fire favor
ttl events expect winner TtlBotEvA
ttl events expect offer TtlBotEvA true
ttl events offerset TtlBotEvA ep_surge,relic,protection
execute as TtlBotEvA run ttl favor choose ep_surge
ttl events expect offer TtlBotEvA false
ttl inspect TtlBotEvB
# Cleanup.
ttl events clear TtlBotEvA
ttl events clear TtlBotEvB
ttl events clear TtlBotEvC
ttl reset TtlBotEvA
ttl reset TtlBotEvB
ttl reset TtlBotEvC
ttlbot remove TtlBotEvA
ttlbot remove TtlBotEvB
ttlbot remove TtlBotEvC
